<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Kansas wheat sales increase.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Kansas wheat sales increase.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cold weather blanketed much of the southern and central U.S. Plains Wendesday, but skies were clear and winds were light, grain dealers said.</p>
<p>Despite the lack of snowcover, dealers doubt the cold will harm the winter wheat. High winds in western Kansas and eastern Colorado Tuesday raised some concerns then, but the winds had died down by Wednesday morning, they said.</p>
<p>Wichita-area wheat sales turned active Tuesday with dealers speculating the cold left farmers with little to do but to sell wheat. As a result, dealers lowered basis bids Wednesday in those areas.</p>
